  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Two-story U-shaped spatial frame from architectural DXF\n\nReconstruct geometry and connectivity from the architectural input.dxf, interpreting its S-* structural lines and labels while filtering the A-* wall, column-footprint and equipment distractors. Reconcile the labelled orthographic views using properties.json dxfMapping. Read supports from properties.json boundaryConditions and the CAD annotations; use the matching member labels in assignments.json and loads.json. Section-detail images describe section properties and roll only. Member local direction follows DXF LINE start-to-end as specified in properties.json; no structural geometry image is supplied. Perform first-order linear elastic analysis using PKPM; save the self-weight OFF and no-rigid-diaphragm settings. Use explicit section/material stiffness and signed right-handed global axes, Z upward. Retain actual load positions and distributed loads.\n\nReport all of the following for each stated selection, with signs and units:\n- Global Uz at the left notch-mouth endpoint n1-2-2 [case-D-D-notch-left-uz]\n- Global Uz at the right notch-mouth endpoint n2-2-2 [case-D-D-notch-right-uz]\n- Global support reaction Fx at left outer-column base n0-0-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-0-Fx]\n- Global support reaction Fy at left outer-column base n0-0-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-0-Fy]\n- Global support reaction Fz at left outer-column base n0-0-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-0-Fz]\n- Global support reaction Mx at left outer-column base n0-0-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-0-Mx]\n- Global support reaction My at left outer-column base n0-0-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-0-My]\n- Global support reaction Mz at left outer-column base n0-0-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-0-Mz]\n- Global support reaction Fx at left outer-column base n0-1-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-1-Fx]\n- Global support reaction Fy at left outer-column base n0-1-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-1-Fy]\n- Global support reaction Fz at left outer-column base n0-1-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-1-Fz]\n- Global support reaction Mx at left outer-column base n0-1-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-1-Mx]\n- Global support reaction My at left outer-column base n0-1-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-1-My]\n- Global support reaction Mz at left outer-column base n0-1-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-1-Mz]\n- Global support reaction Fx at left outer-column base n0-2-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-2-Fx]\n- Global support reaction Fy at left outer-column base n0-2-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-2-Fy]\n- Global support reaction Fz at left outer-column base n0-2-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-2-Fz]\n- Global support reaction Mx at left outer-column base n0-2-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-2-Mx]\n- Global support reaction My at left outer-column base n0-2-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-2-My]\n- Global support reaction Mz at left outer-column base n0-2-0 [case-D-D-left-outer-2-Mz]\n\nProvide labelled model and result figures consistent with the numerical values. Preserve the input-to-model ID mapping, engine version/settings, current execution log, original result tables and figure data. If an essential datum is missing, ask specifically for it before analysis.\n",
      "state": 1,
